{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,2]],"date-time":"2024-10-02T04:15:36Z","timestamp":1727842536114},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"The Journal of Political Philosophy and Sociology of Politics","issue":"3","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["JPPSP"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,24]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>The literature on political trust currently continues to be dominated by the cognitive approach, whose adherents perceive trust as a function of political knowledge and social experience. In turn, the psycho-emotional foundations of political trust (personality traits, psychological needs and emotions) are still in the shadow of the cognitive revolution and remain poorly understood. The article attempts to justify the need to study political trust not only as a rational-evaluative construct, but also as a complex psycho-emotional phenomenon that arises at the intersection of cognitive and affective processes occurring at the conscious and subconscious levels.  Having consistently analyzed three approaches to understanding the nature of political trust \u2014 as knowledge, as heuristics and as affect \u2014 the author elaborates his definition of this phenomenon, describing it as a specific psycho-emotional state that accumulates knowledge about objects of political space, emotionally and symbolically significant images of politicians and institutions formed in the process of socialization, as well as the confidence that the expectations arising on this basis will be met to one degree or another in the future. Moving from the conceptual to the empirical level, he examines survey and experimental strategies for distinguishing between cognitive and affective foundations of trust, revealing their possibilities and limitations.  The final part of the article outlines potential further directions for research in the field of political trust. According to the author, agent-based modeling is extremely promising in this regard, as it allows looking at the cognitive and affective bases of political trust as a single whole, where cognitive and affective processes are closely interconnected and capable of moving from one state to another.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.30570\/2078-5089-2024-114-3-82-108","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,1]],"date-time":"2024-10-01T12:51:12Z","timestamp":1727787072000},"page":"82-108","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Between \u201cRatio\u201d and \u201cIrratio\u201d: in Search of an Optimal Strategy for Studying Trust in Political Space"],"prefix":"10.30570","volume":"114","author":[{"given":"V. V.","family":"Sychev","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"12010","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,24]]},"container-title":["The Journal of Political Theory, Political Philosophy and Sociology of Politics Politeia"],"original-title":["\u041c\u0435\u0436\u0434\u0443 \u00abratio\u00bb \u0438 \u00abirratio\u00bb: \u0432 \u043f\u043e\u0438\u0441\u043a\u0430\u0445 \u043e\u043f\u0442\u0438\u043c\u0430\u043b\u044c\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u0441\u0442\u0440\u0430\u0442\u0435\u0433\u0438\u0438 \u0438\u0437\u0443\u0447\u0435\u043d\u0438\u044f \u0434\u043e\u0432\u0435\u0440\u0438\u044f \u0432 \u043f\u043e\u043b\u0438\u0442\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0441\u043a\u043e\u043c \u043f\u0440\u043e\u0441\u0442\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0441\u0442\u0432\u0435"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,1]],"date-time":"2024-10-01T12:51:17Z","timestamp":1727787077000},"score":1,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/politeia.ru\/files\/articles\/eng\/Politeia-2024-3(114)-Pages-001-196-82-108.pdf"}},"subtitle":[],"short-title":[],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,24]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"3","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,24]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,24]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.30570\/2078-5089-2024-114-3-82-108","relation":{},"ISSN":["2078-5089","2587-5914"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2078-5089","type":"print"},{"value":"2587-5914","type":"electronic"}],"subject":[],"published":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,24]]}}}